# Code owners -- a change to any path below REQUIRES the maintainer's review before it can merge.
# Pair this with a branch ruleset on `main` that has "Require review from Code Owners" enabled.
# These are the supply-chain-critical surfaces: the CI/release workflows, the build scripts, and the installer.
#
# NOTE: @adiazpar is the maintainer's GitHub handle -- verify it matches the account that owns the repo
# (an invalid handle here is silently ignored by GitHub, i.e. no enforcement).

/.github/      @adiazpar
*.ps1          @adiazpar
/installer/    @adiazpar

# The release tooling the workflows EXECUTE. prepare-release.yml is owner-guarded
# by /.github/ above, but it runs `python3 tools/draft_changelog.py` in the one
# job that holds ANTHROPIC_API_KEY -- so without this line a contributor could
# change what that job runs, and the prompt it runs with, without an owner ever
# seeing it. tools/requirements.txt pins the drafter's dependencies by hash and
# is the same class of surface.
/tools/        @adiazpar
